## The idea

Counts only ever change by **one**. So group keys into **buckets by count**, and keep the buckets in a doubly linked list sorted by count. Inc moves a key to the next bucket (creating it if missing); Dec moves it to the previous one. The first bucket holds a minimum key and the last bucket a maximum key — no sorting, no heap, everything O(1). One lock around each method makes it thread-safe.

## Step by step

1. Keep: a LinkedList of buckets (each bucket = a count and a set of keys), and a dictionary key → its bucket node.
2. Inc(new key): put it in the first bucket if that bucket's count is 1, otherwise create a count-1 bucket at the front.
3. Inc(existing key): the target is the next bucket if its count is current+1; otherwise insert a new bucket right after. Move the key; delete the old bucket if it became empty.
4. Dec: the same, moving to the previous bucket; at count 1 the key is removed completely. Dec of an absent key does nothing.
5. GetMaxKey / GetMinKey: any key from the last / first bucket, or "" when empty.

## Worked example

**Input:** Inc hello, Inc hello, Inc leet, then Dec hello twice

| Step | What happens |
|---|---|
| Inc hello | buckets: [1:{hello}] |
| Inc hello | hello moves to a new count-2 bucket → [2:{hello}] (count-1 bucket emptied and removed) |
| Inc leet | new count-1 bucket at the front → [1:{leet}] ⇄ [2:{hello}] |
| max / min | last bucket → hello; first bucket → leet |
| Dec hello ×2 | hello → count 1 → then removed → [1:{leet}] |

**Result:** max = hello, min = leet; after the Decs, max = min = leet

## Cost

Every operation O(1). Memory O(number of keys).

## The code (C#, compiled and tested against every part of the question)

```csharp
public class AllOne {
    private class Bucket {
        public int Count;
        public HashSet<string> Keys = new HashSet<string>();
    }

    private readonly LinkedList<Bucket> _buckets = new LinkedList<Bucket>();     // sorted by Count, ascending
    private readonly Dictionary<string, LinkedListNode<Bucket>> _bucketOf = new Dictionary<string, LinkedListNode<Bucket>>();
    private readonly object _lock = new object();

    public void Inc(string key) {
        lock (_lock) {
            LinkedListNode<Bucket> current;
            if (!_bucketOf.TryGetValue(key, out current)) {
                // new key: it belongs in a count-1 bucket at the very front
                LinkedListNode<Bucket> first = _buckets.First;
                if (first == null || first.Value.Count != 1) {
                    first = _buckets.AddFirst(new Bucket { Count = 1 });
                }
                first.Value.Keys.Add(key);
                _bucketOf[key] = first;
                return;
            }
            // existing key: move it to the bucket with Count + 1
            LinkedListNode<Bucket> next = current.Next;
            if (next == null || next.Value.Count != current.Value.Count + 1) {
                next = _buckets.AddAfter(current, new Bucket { Count = current.Value.Count + 1 });
            }
            next.Value.Keys.Add(key);
            _bucketOf[key] = next;
            RemoveKeyFromBucket(current, key);
        }
    }

    public void Dec(string key) {
        lock (_lock) {
            LinkedListNode<Bucket> current;
            if (!_bucketOf.TryGetValue(key, out current)) return;    // absent key: nothing to do
            if (current.Value.Count == 1) {                         // count reaches 0: forget the key
                _bucketOf.Remove(key);
                RemoveKeyFromBucket(current, key);
                return;
            }
            LinkedListNode<Bucket> previous = current.Previous;
            if (previous == null || previous.Value.Count != current.Value.Count - 1) {
                previous = _buckets.AddBefore(current, new Bucket { Count = current.Value.Count - 1 });
            }
            previous.Value.Keys.Add(key);
            _bucketOf[key] = previous;
            RemoveKeyFromBucket(current, key);
        }
    }

    public string GetMaxKey() {
        lock (_lock) {
            if (_buckets.Last == null) return "";
            return AnyKey(_buckets.Last.Value);
        }
    }

    public string GetMinKey() {
        lock (_lock) {
            if (_buckets.First == null) return "";
            return AnyKey(_buckets.First.Value);
        }
    }

    private void RemoveKeyFromBucket(LinkedListNode<Bucket> node, string key) {
        node.Value.Keys.Remove(key);
        if (node.Value.Keys.Count == 0) _buckets.Remove(node);      // never keep empty buckets
    }

    private static string AnyKey(Bucket bucket) {
        foreach (string key in bucket.Keys) return key;
        return "";
    }
}
